# Cover inspection

The world's image-generation resource returned HTTP 200 with a server-sent event
response. The request specified gpt-image-2, medium quality, 1536×1024; the decoded
source actually measures 2070×760 pixels. The retained source and nonsecret request
and response metadata accompany the generator.

Both `cover_source.png` and the final `../report/cover.png` were opened and visually
inspected. Navy curves, teal and amber strips, and sampling nodes remain legible
on an ivory background. There is no text, axis, or legend. These are decorative
forms, not measured quadrature results.

The generator crops the central 2070×318 strip (top pixel 221), then resizes it to
1950×300 pixels. The final panoramic crop preserves the curves, strips and nodes;
no labels or scientific claims depend on the artwork. The report owner can place
it at 6.5×1 inches or proportionally smaller.
